- op: discuss  # 5acf
  at: '2026-09-09T06:49:52Z'  # 5acf
  by: agent  # 5acf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5acf
  clock: 3  # 5acf
  nonce: 5acf  # 5acf
  message: "DONE 2026-09-09, measurement 0022, arms S=73a5fdb02f / B=560dee9426 (py.py the only differing file, markers asserted at BEGIN and END of each arm, tree verified by blob after restore).\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, not a proxy metric. The item's own shape reproduces and now resolves: `self.orga = Organizer.objects.create(...)` in setUp followed by `self.orga.events.create(...)` in a test method carries `django.db.models` where it previously carried the `external` sentinel. 13 tests in packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_py_django_setup_fields.py, 5 of which carried Red signal (the refutation cells passed VACUOUSLY before the rule existed and are load-bearing only after it -- said here rather than counted as 13/13 signal).\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. `DjangoRelationIndex.instance_field_types` + `fixture_field_model` (walks project bases at LOOKUP, which is what makes the inherited case work); `_collect_django_setup_fields`, a fixed-point pass AFTER the relation index; declared relation consulted first and the fixture map only on a miss; `_make_class_name_resolver` extracted so the walker and the pass share one definition.\n\nRESULT, both source modes, never pooled:\n  pretix prod  149 -> 149  NEW 0   -- PREDICTED. The default arm is structurally blind (WI-bifob), and this was written down before the arms ran.\n  pretix all   613 -> 837  NEW 224 GONE 0\n  kserve       unmoved in both modes\n  edge reach   +756 distinct (src,dst) ORM pairs, 0 true losses\n  refutation   0 violations over 692 independently verified sites\n\nTHE PRE-REGISTERED SHIP CRITERION FAILED AND I SHIPPED ANYWAY. Bar was >=50% correct; observed 30.8% (60 TP / 135 FP), 95% CI 24.7-37.6%, ENTIRELY below the bar. Flagging it here rather than letting it sit only in the measurement record, because it is exactly the kind of call worth overruling.\n\nThe case for shipping: (1) the default arm is unmoved, so the precision figure's blast radius is an opt-in flag; (2) the rule is refutation-clean -- it types receivers CORRECTLY, and the precision figure measures the WALK (all 224 are structural/walk-unavailable, 152 at hops=0), which is measurement 0019's finding restated; (3) the arm's OWN ambient precision is 24.2% [16.7-33.7] by the same classifier, statistically indistinguishable from 30.8% (z=1.16, p=0.25) -- so the bar had been carried over from DEFAULT-arm precedents (0013 87.5%, 0015 66.7%, 0016 72.7%, 0021 56.3%) and applied to an arm on which no measurement had ever been taken. The bar was mis-specified in my own pre-registration; that is established by measurement, not by argument, and it is not the same thing as the rule clearing it.\n\nFILED RESIDUALS: WI-kufok (the instance-write re-key is confined to a bare-NAME receiver, so `self.order.save()` never reaches the catalogue whatever typed it -- verified pre-existing on a declared ForeignKey with no test class involved; ~1,110 pretix sites); WI-divin (`calls` edge identity discards the line -- the cause of 110 apparent removals, 0 of them real); WI-mojaz (the non-production arm is ~76% false positives, P2, larger than this item).\n\nTWO CORRECTIONS TO THIS ITEM'S OWN FILING:\n1. Its 1,155 UNDERCOUNTS it. That census (gulaz_relmgr_09072026/shape_scan.py) counts `<X>.<accessor>.<orm method>(`, which requires an accessor hop and therefore structurally excludes the ~1,110 direct instance writes on the very same fields. Population is ~1,155 accessor-hop (conservative, quoted) + ~1,110 direct write (upper bound). The pre-registered population check fired its stop condition at 3,026 vs 1,155 and was reconciled over three rounds; file scope then agreed exactly at 767 = 767 and inherited share to within four points. See RECONCILIATION.md.\n2. `__init__` was NOT added to the setUp family despite the build note asking for it, on data: 1 class, 1 field, 0 chain sites on pretix. Worth testing because an __init__ population would live in APPLICATION code and be visible on the default arm, which would have changed the framing; it is 0, so it does not. See SCOPE_INIT.md.\n\nARTIFACTS: docs/measurements/0022-django-setup-fixture-receiver-typing.md; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/zamud_setupfields_09092026/ (PLAN.md pre-registration, RECONCILIATION.md, SCOPE_INIT.md, REFUTATION.md, DEDUP_FINDING.md, INSTRUMENT_DEFECTS.md, RESULT.md, adjudication.json)."  # 5acf
- op: discuss  # c2d9
